sentences.l:
So he in the huts, Menoetius’ sturdy son,
was healing Eurypylus, struck; and they fought,
Argives and Trojans, in a throng;

and to the gods they gave not famous hecatombs,
so that for them the swift ships and the plentiful spoil,
holding them within, it might protect;

and smooth he made them along the strong-flowing Hellespont,
and again the great beach with sands he covered,
the wall having wiped out;

but then around fighting and shouting was ablaze
the well-built wall, and rang the timbers of the towers
being struck;

and the Argives, by the whip of Zeus overcome,
at the hollow ships hemmed in, held themselves back,
fearing Hector, strong counsellor of flight;

and they, tower-wise themselves having arrayed,
face it and stand and hurl thickset
spears from their hands;

and not for him the horses
dared, the swift-footed, but loudly they whinnied on the topmost
lip, standing upon it;

for scared them off the ditch,
wide, and neither to leap over from near nor to cross
easy;

the horses, let the attendants hold back at the ditch,
and ourselves, the foot-soldiers, with our armour armed,
let us all follow Hector, in a close mass;
